WEBVTT

00:01.390 --> 00:02.980
Good morning.

00:02.980 --> 00:05.480
Kyoko. Kyoko.

00:06.010 --> 00:08.520
Miyamura-kun's here to 
take you to school, Kyoko.

00:08.520 --> 00:10.340
Good morning, Hori-san.

00:11.340 --> 00:14.090
It was your idea to walk together.

00:14.960 --> 00:17.740
You said we should leave early.

00:17.740 --> 00:21.240
You were watching that horror special
into the wee hours of the morning.

00:23.830 --> 00:25.530
Go get changed.

00:27.110 --> 00:28.800
And wash your face, too.

00:32.300 --> 00:34.490
Hey, Miyamura-kun, want some coffee?

00:34.490 --> 00:36.900
Oh, thank you.

00:37.290 --> 00:39.590
<i>This is where the alleged murder took place.</i>

00:39.590 --> 00:41.470
Where did that happen?

00:39.590 --> 00:43.130
<i>Police are attempting to locate 
the victim's younger brother,</i>

00:41.470 --> 00:44.530
A neighboring prefecture. How scary.

00:43.130 --> 00:45.640
<i>who may have information 
pertinent to the case.</i>

00:48.220 --> 00:49.530
<i>For our next story...</i>

00:50.730 --> 00:52.860
<i>Now for today's weather.</i>

00:50.730 --> 00:53.920
Man, it's cold.

00:52.890 --> 00:55.360
<i>Most of the country will have clear skies,</i>

00:55.360 --> 00:58.410
<i>and cold northerly winds 
will largely be kept at bay.</i>

00:56.470 --> 00:58.410
Thank you for the food.

00:58.410 --> 01:01.320
<i>Northern Japan will see 
unseasonably warm temperatures.</i>

01:00.440 --> 01:02.160
<b>She hasn't come back...</b>

01:00.650 --> 01:02.160
<i>She hasn't come back!</i>

01:02.160 --> 01:04.870
<i>The east will see average
or above average temperatures.</i>

01:03.310 --> 01:06.570
Um, could I go knock on her door?

01:04.870 --> 01:08.680
<i>Western Japan, Okinawa, and the Amami 
Islands will see normal temperatures.</i>

01:06.570 --> 01:07.700
Sure.

01:08.500 --> 01:10.560
Wait, she hasn't come back yet?

01:12.580 --> 01:13.670
Hori-san?

01:14.190 --> 01:15.600
Hori-san, I'm coming in.

01:18.190 --> 01:20.080
<i>She fell back to sleep...</i>

01:20.330 --> 01:24.310
You're asleep! You're asleep! Wake up!

01:25.050 --> 01:27.600
Are you going to go 
without brushing your hair?

01:27.600 --> 01:28.780
No.

01:28.780 --> 01:32.420
In that case, get up and turn around.

01:48.030 --> 01:50.860
Hori-san, Hori-san! We're gonna be late.

01:52.570 --> 01:54.240
Gotta go to the bathroom...

01:54.240 --> 01:56.840
Okay, I'll put on my shoes and wait for you.

01:58.340 --> 01:59.340
See you!

01:59.860 --> 02:02.070
Yeah. Have a good day.

02:08.010 --> 02:09.230
M-Miyamura!

02:09.230 --> 02:11.890
<b>Styled</b>

02:09.650 --> 02:11.220
What happened to my hair?!

02:12.170 --> 02:14.850
Well, it was a mess...

02:14.850 --> 02:17.380
I look like I'm going to a party!

02:17.380 --> 02:19.590
I didn't think I could get
the ponytail right.

02:19.590 --> 02:20.780
Oh, man!

02:20.780 --> 02:22.200
Are you gonna take it down?

02:22.200 --> 02:24.060
It doesn't go with my uniform!

02:25.480 --> 02:26.790
So you're gonna take it down?

02:29.460 --> 02:32.430
D-Does it look good?

02:32.820 --> 02:39.330
<b>It's not about how good it looks. I don't really know how
 to do hair, but I worked really hard to make it nice
 anyway, so I don't want it to just go to waste.</b>

02:39.880 --> 02:40.680
Yeah.

02:41.510 --> 02:43.550
Fine, I'll keep it like this.

02:43.550 --> 02:44.840
Yay!

02:45.960 --> 02:47.970
So it's okay? It's not weird, is it?

02:47.970 --> 02:49.190
No, it's not weird.

02:49.190 --> 02:51.060
It's really cute.

02:51.060 --> 02:52.660
<i>I'm cute?</i>

02:53.290 --> 02:56.710
<i>I didn't know I was so good at buns.</i>

04:29.990 --> 04:32.020
Hori, you look so cute!

04:32.020 --> 04:34.360
I want a bun, too!

04:34.360 --> 04:37.010
Hey, lookin' good. Did you do that yourself?

04:37.520 --> 04:38.390
Like it?

04:38.390 --> 04:39.880
I might try one, too.

04:40.140 --> 04:43.110
I'm not sure your hair is long enough.

04:43.110 --> 04:44.660
What? It's not?

04:44.660 --> 04:45.980
He's right.

04:45.980 --> 04:47.640
Oh...

04:49.440 --> 04:51.580
Kyon-Kyon, that's so cute!

04:51.580 --> 04:53.090
What's the occasion?

04:53.090 --> 04:54.480
Nothing special.

04:54.480 --> 04:56.920
Did you have a change 
of heart about something?

04:55.020 --> 04:56.920
<i>Her hair is probably too fine.</i>

04:57.450 --> 05:00.650
No, no, I just felt like it.

04:57.780 --> 05:00.650
Hey, what are you staring at?

05:00.650 --> 05:02.770
I figured it might be nice for a change.

05:01.270 --> 05:03.140
Wh-What?

05:02.770 --> 05:05.440
It's great! Are you gonna change your image?

05:03.140 --> 05:06.680
President... you don't have enough.

05:05.440 --> 05:06.740
I might not be ready for that.

05:06.680 --> 05:08.130
It wouldn't work out.

05:08.130 --> 05:09.910
Am I lacking in something?!

05:10.410 --> 05:12.810
<i>Oh, Kono-san...</i>

05:12.810 --> 05:17.110
<b>Tied to the side</b>

05:13.440 --> 05:16.450
<i>That might look better than a bun.</i>

05:17.000 --> 05:18.440
<i>Everyone's different.</i>

05:18.440 --> 05:20.140
Thanks for waiting!

05:20.140 --> 05:22.400
Everyone's been complimenting my hair.

05:22.400 --> 05:23.920
Of course.

05:24.580 --> 05:26.330
You look cute.

05:26.700 --> 05:29.520
You're really the cutest of all.

05:26.700 --> 05:30.210
<b><i>BLUUUSH</i></b>

05:30.180 --> 05:31.170
Ouch!

05:31.170 --> 05:32.830
<i>Senseless violence!</i>

05:33.620 --> 05:35.710
You can do my hair again sometime.

05:37.490 --> 05:39.880
Maybe I'll try a braid next time.

05:39.880 --> 05:42.940
<i>Does she like the bun?</i>

05:40.250 --> 05:42.940
Oh, can you handle that?

05:43.960 --> 05:46.050
My neck feels cold.

05:46.050 --> 05:47.470
Does it?

05:47.610 --> 05:48.950
<b>Pom</b>

05:48.970 --> 05:50.670
You'll ruin it!

05:51.280 --> 05:52.950
<i>What are they doing?</i>

05:53.980 --> 05:56.140
I can't stand how silky Miyamura's hair is.

05:56.140 --> 05:58.890
It doesn't stick up funny, 
and a comb passes right through it.

05:58.890 --> 06:01.090
Is that so?

06:02.000 --> 06:04.170
I'm just so jealous!

06:04.170 --> 06:07.130
If it never sticks up funny, then make it.

06:07.500 --> 06:10.370
So your solution is
"if there's no bread, just eat cake"?

06:10.370 --> 06:14.580
I mean, if you tie hair up,
it kinda holds like that for a while, right?

06:14.580 --> 06:17.340
It'd only be temporary,
but you could try that.

06:17.340 --> 06:18.180
I get it!

06:18.180 --> 06:20.610
That's easier than using a hair iron.

06:20.610 --> 06:22.860
Don't go overboard, Kyo-chan...

06:25.230 --> 06:27.010
<b>Ting</b>

06:27.010 --> 06:28.170
All done!

06:28.170 --> 06:30.270
What did I do to deserve this?

06:40.160 --> 06:42.050
There.

06:43.010 --> 06:44.550
That should do it.

06:44.550 --> 06:46.670
Thank you, Sengoku-kun.

06:46.670 --> 06:48.810
Oh, it was nothing.

06:49.340 --> 06:52.830
I thought we were keeping things organized,

06:52.830 --> 06:55.880
but I guess we had more
things than we thought.

06:55.880 --> 06:59.120
We're constantly getting 
more papers and stuff.

06:59.900 --> 07:01.270
But I must say...

07:03.540 --> 07:07.450
I was surprised to see you up on 
a chair cleaning the top of the cabinets.

07:07.450 --> 07:08.580
You could've gotten hurt.

07:08.580 --> 07:11.530
But I wanted to dust up there.

07:12.230 --> 07:13.670
You don't like dust?

07:13.670 --> 07:17.040
Yoshikawa-kun and Iura-kun 
have been coughing sometimes.

07:17.040 --> 07:18.660
I thought it might be the dust.

07:18.660 --> 07:21.120
Did I catch you in the middle
of talking about my awesomeness?

07:21.120 --> 07:22.230
No, you didn't.

07:22.230 --> 07:22.920
You did not.

07:22.920 --> 07:24.280
No?!

07:24.280 --> 07:25.670
Are you organizing stuff?

07:25.670 --> 07:30.010
Yeah, since we won't be 
using this room much longer.

07:30.010 --> 07:32.800
Hey, this box looks like it might fall.

07:32.800 --> 07:35.300
Oh, Sengoku-kun just put it...

07:35.300 --> 07:37.490
I'll take it down for now.

07:37.490 --> 07:39.810
Does this go on top of the cabinet, too?

07:40.250 --> 07:43.100
Ah, th-thank you!

07:43.100 --> 07:44.250
That's a big help—

07:47.300 --> 07:51.080
I know Ishikawa-kun's gotten 
strong by doing sports,

07:51.080 --> 07:52.730
but what about you, Iura-kun?

07:52.730 --> 07:54.850
Where did you get that extra muscle?

07:54.850 --> 07:57.870
Maybe from helping my 
grandpa move furniture.

07:57.870 --> 07:59.120
Furniture?!

07:59.120 --> 08:01.050
I took out the trash.

08:01.050 --> 08:02.510
Welcome back, Remi—

08:02.040 --> 08:05.130
Stare...

08:03.110 --> 08:04.100
Hori-san?

08:04.430 --> 08:05.610
Huh?

08:06.270 --> 08:09.020
Ayasaki-san was throwing 
things away in random bins.

08:09.020 --> 08:11.420
Next time, separate the recyclables 
before you give it to her.

08:11.420 --> 08:12.220
Remi!

08:12.220 --> 08:14.240
I'm sorry, Kyon-Kyon!

08:14.240 --> 08:17.780
Thank you for helping her, Hori-san.

08:17.780 --> 08:21.200
I don't think there will be 
a next time, though.

08:21.610 --> 08:23.250
I guess you're right.

08:23.250 --> 08:25.020
Is Ayasaki-san around?

08:25.020 --> 08:26.560
Oh, everyone's here.

08:26.560 --> 08:30.480
What is it? Do you need me 
for something, Yanagin?

08:30.480 --> 08:35.230
N-No, I just found a cell phone 
I recognized in the trash area.

08:35.230 --> 08:38.660
I saw you put it down without looking
 when we were throwing stuff away.

08:38.660 --> 08:39.910
Oh!

08:39.910 --> 08:41.460
Thanks, Yanagin!

08:41.460 --> 08:42.340
It's nothing.

08:42.820 --> 08:44.760
Are you organizing in here?

08:44.760 --> 08:45.720
I can help.

08:45.720 --> 08:48.460
Yanagi-kun, this stuff is pretty heavy—

08:48.460 --> 08:51.960
Someone might trip on this,
so I'll move it over to the corner.

08:52.770 --> 08:54.990
Miyamura-kun, I need you here!

08:54.990 --> 08:55.940
What's with him?

08:55.940 --> 08:59.120
He wants someone weaker than him here
to make him feel better.

08:59.120 --> 09:01.600
What a small man.

09:02.270 --> 09:03.250
You called?

09:03.250 --> 09:05.850
Whoa, he's carrying something
that looks heavy!

09:06.260 --> 09:08.980
Miyamura-kun, what is that? 
What're you doing with it?

09:08.980 --> 09:11.350
Yasuda told me to take it.

09:11.350 --> 09:14.880
He's giving back everything he's 
confiscated during the school year.

09:14.880 --> 09:17.210
Oh, like magazines and stuff.

09:17.610 --> 09:21.070
Yasuda couldn't carry it himself.

09:20.810 --> 09:25.580
<b>Me & Yasuda (?) ← Yanagi-kun ← Miyamura-kun ← Iura-kun ← Ishikawa-kun</b>

09:20.810 --> 09:26.870
<b>Muscle & Strength Ranking (Tentative)</b>

09:21.440 --> 09:24.120
<b>Depressed</b>

09:21.870 --> 09:24.790
Well, there's not <i>that</i> big 
a difference between us all.

09:24.790 --> 09:26.060
Oh?

09:25.580 --> 09:26.870
<b>Me & Yasuda (?) ← Yanagi-kun ← Miyamura-kun ← Iura-kun ← Ishikawa-kun ← Kyo-chan (Hall of Fame)</b>

09:26.060 --> 09:28.560
The hall-of-famer is saying something.

09:28.560 --> 09:29.650
What?

09:29.650 --> 09:32.590
Sengoku-kun is fine the way he is!

09:32.590 --> 09:36.370
I'll get stronger for him!

09:36.370 --> 09:38.120
You're amazing, Remi.

09:38.120 --> 09:44.160
R-Remi, I appreciate it,
but I like you the way you are, too.

09:44.160 --> 09:45.390
Hey...

09:45.800 --> 09:48.680
Yasuda made me bring this here.

09:48.680 --> 09:51.550
Is Yasuda even weaker than Yoshikawa?!

09:51.550 --> 09:54.040
Yoshikawa-san, I'll take that!

09:54.040 --> 09:56.220
Thanks, Yanagi-kun.

09:56.870 --> 09:58.400
This is quite heavy.

09:58.400 --> 09:59.930
Yanagi-kun, be careful!

10:00.430 --> 10:02.170
Chagrin...

10:02.170 --> 10:03.710
Are you okay?

10:02.240 --> 10:05.910
<b>Muscle & Strength Ranking</b>

10:02.240 --> 10:05.910
<b>Miyamura-kun & Yanagi-kun 
↓ 
Yoshikawa-san
 ↓ 
Me & Yasuda
(Confirmed)</b>

10:04.200 --> 10:05.910
<i>Now I feel sorry for him.</i>

10:06.410 --> 10:09.000
Hey, the heavy stuff is all on one side.

10:09.000 --> 10:10.750
That'd make it hard to carry.

10:10.750 --> 10:12.270
I'd probably drop it, too.

10:14.120 --> 10:15.210
Thanks, guys...

10:16.660 --> 10:18.580
There's a postcard in here.

10:18.580 --> 10:21.090
It was probably stuck in a magazine.

10:21.090 --> 10:22.630
Maybe this one.

10:23.220 --> 10:25.300
Hey, grab that pile.

10:25.300 --> 10:27.690
Oh, I haven't seen this in forever!

10:27.690 --> 10:29.890
Miyamura, once we're done...

10:29.890 --> 10:30.900
Yeah.

10:43.230 --> 10:45.300
What's wrong, Iura?

10:45.300 --> 10:47.840
Sengoku, don't start reading it!

10:47.840 --> 10:49.770
But doesn't it take you back?

10:51.360 --> 10:52.940
I think...

10:52.940 --> 10:54.790
I want to go to the beach.

10:56.030 --> 10:58.710
That's right! We were talking about going.

10:58.710 --> 11:01.230
Indeed! Someone can get
 a license and drive us.

11:01.230 --> 11:03.430
In a car? Awesome!

11:03.430 --> 11:06.310
Our troop will have fun 
no matter where we go!

11:05.850 --> 11:17.940
<b>Graduation</b>

11:06.310 --> 11:07.260
Don't call us a troop.

11:07.260 --> 11:08.300
Are we ants?

11:08.300 --> 11:10.580
Iura-kun, how about "group" instead?

11:10.580 --> 11:13.430
Yeah, hey, hey! That's it, Akane!

11:22.490 --> 11:25.490
<b>Karaoke</b>

11:24.930 --> 11:26.070
I know, right?

11:26.070 --> 11:28.470
Wanna check out that shop 
we saw in the magazine?

11:28.470 --> 11:29.740
Wait, for real?

11:29.740 --> 11:30.700
Yeah!

11:30.700 --> 11:31.420
Let's go!

11:31.420 --> 11:34.500
Sota, what do you want to eat today?

11:34.990 --> 11:36.120
A rice omelet!

11:36.120 --> 11:37.950
What, again?

11:37.950 --> 11:39.360
Yep, again!

11:40.870 --> 11:43.760
I wonder if we still have ketchup...

11:45.360 --> 11:46.260
Kyo-chan.

11:46.260 --> 11:47.760
<b>Mathematics II</b>

11:49.680 --> 11:50.720
Thanks.

11:50.720 --> 11:52.850
You're finally giving it back!

11:52.850 --> 11:55.140
You said you wouldn't have math today.

11:55.810 --> 11:58.930
You're supposed to give it back 
right after class ends.

11:58.930 --> 11:59.780
Um...

12:00.550 --> 12:05.150
Sengoku-kun was helping 
the teacher after class.

12:05.150 --> 12:07.470
Oh, I see.

12:07.470 --> 12:08.730
That makes sense.

12:08.730 --> 12:09.660
See you.

12:10.210 --> 12:11.410
Yeah.

12:13.290 --> 12:15.010
Oh, Hori!

12:15.860 --> 12:18.180
Are you free after school?

12:18.590 --> 12:20.060
Um...

12:21.280 --> 12:23.670
Hori likes to go straight home after school.

12:23.670 --> 12:24.810
Right?

12:25.280 --> 12:26.850
Yeah, sorry.

12:26.850 --> 12:28.900
Oh, okay. No worries.

12:28.900 --> 12:31.440
Some of us are getting together to hang out,

12:31.440 --> 12:33.310
so I was wondering if you wanted in.

12:33.310 --> 12:35.060
That's all.

12:36.170 --> 12:38.560
Looks like it's just us!

12:42.150 --> 12:45.360
Toru really likes you, y'know?

12:45.360 --> 12:48.930
Oh, come on. He just invited me to hang out.

12:48.930 --> 12:51.550
Yeah, but how many times does that make?

12:51.550 --> 12:54.240
You get invited out all the time.

12:54.240 --> 12:57.540
I'm just there to increase the headcount.

13:02.860 --> 13:03.700
What?

13:03.700 --> 13:04.650
It's so windy!

13:04.650 --> 13:05.700
That scared me!

13:14.610 --> 13:17.470
Maybe I'll close the window.

13:17.470 --> 13:18.490
Yeah.

13:22.110 --> 13:24.360
The next thing I knew,
she was wearing the same shoes.

13:24.360 --> 13:26.900
The heck?! <i>That's</i> how she's 
trying to get friendly with you?

13:26.900 --> 13:28.770
I just pretended not to notice.

13:28.770 --> 13:30.110
That's what I'd do.

13:30.110 --> 13:30.820
And then...

13:30.820 --> 13:31.990
Oh, sorry.

13:31.990 --> 13:33.330
No, I was...

13:33.330 --> 13:36.370
And then, even with the same shoes, 
she starts a fight with me.

13:36.370 --> 13:38.120
Huh? Why?

13:38.120 --> 13:40.000
Get this... It was about takoyaki.

13:40.000 --> 13:40.620
Huh?!

13:45.160 --> 13:47.540
Sorry we ran into you.

13:47.540 --> 13:50.380
No, it's okay. Thank you.

13:51.990 --> 13:53.640
Are you on the student council?

13:54.260 --> 13:55.150
Yeah.

13:55.640 --> 13:57.040
Must be a lot of work.

13:57.040 --> 13:58.620
It's nothing but odd jobs.

14:05.540 --> 14:07.790
<i>There's someone on the roof.</i>

14:09.590 --> 14:11.660
<i>I bet it's nice up there.</i>

14:12.250 --> 14:14.240
<i>Not that I have any business going.</i>

14:15.780 --> 14:17.670
It's so cold!

14:18.160 --> 14:19.420
Hurry up!

14:23.980 --> 14:25.420
<i>Wow...</i>

14:25.880 --> 14:28.420
<i>That guy has no intention 
of participating whatsoever.</i>

14:29.570 --> 14:31.110
Hori!

14:31.110 --> 14:32.370
Yeah.

14:33.430 --> 14:34.930
Student Council

14:34.100 --> 14:34.920
Here.

14:34.930 --> 14:36.930
<i>Skull Ninja
</i>Konoha

14:35.300 --> 14:36.930
Thank you!

14:36.930 --> 14:40.020
Sengoku said you'd have a copy.

14:41.510 --> 14:43.900
There are more in the student council room.

14:43.900 --> 14:45.090
Help yourself anytime.

14:45.090 --> 14:48.390
Manga isn't allowed in school, so 
the student council shouldn't have any!

14:48.390 --> 14:49.430
But I'll still borrow it.

14:49.430 --> 14:50.850
It'll be our secret.

14:50.850 --> 14:52.450
Oh, Hori-san.

14:52.880 --> 14:54.720
What are you guys up to?

14:54.720 --> 14:57.180
I'm borrowing a book from Kono-san.

14:57.180 --> 14:58.700
It's manga, though.

15:01.200 --> 15:03.830
Really? You can come today?

15:03.830 --> 15:04.810
Yep.

15:04.810 --> 15:07.680
Great! I'll invite Shu, too.

15:05.020 --> 15:07.100
<i>Mama's coming home early today.</i>

15:21.380 --> 15:23.420
I'm gonna sing my heart out!

15:23.420 --> 15:25.220
Just don't hog the mic.

15:24.100 --> 15:25.580
What's wrong, Kyo-chan?

15:25.220 --> 15:26.530
Karaoke...

15:26.530 --> 15:28.110
You're coming, right, Sakura?

15:27.020 --> 15:30.420
I get the feeling that we're missing someone.

15:28.110 --> 15:30.150
Maybe just to listen.

15:30.150 --> 15:32.610
But you sing anime songs while
cleaning the council room.

15:31.820 --> 15:32.610
Oh.

15:32.610 --> 15:34.860
How do you know that?!

15:33.070 --> 15:34.860
Yanagi!

15:35.870 --> 15:38.750
We got to be friends in our elective class.

15:38.750 --> 15:40.310
Thank you for having me.

15:40.310 --> 15:42.260
If he's bothering you, just tell us.

15:42.260 --> 15:43.650
Yeah, spill it.

15:43.650 --> 15:45.620
How would I be bothering him?

15:45.620 --> 15:48.000
H-He's not bothering me at all!

15:56.930 --> 15:58.050
Bye-bye.

15:58.050 --> 15:59.760
See you tomorrow.

16:03.120 --> 16:05.640
Crap, my phone...

16:09.830 --> 16:11.650
<i>Um, what's his name?</i>

16:14.330 --> 16:16.530
<i>Never mind. I'll get it myself.</i>

16:31.020 --> 16:32.240
Here.

16:32.240 --> 16:34.260
Th-Thank you.

16:44.560 --> 16:47.560
We found each other

16:50.300 --> 16:52.470
Hey, Miyamura...

16:59.200 --> 17:00.320
Hmm?

17:00.880 --> 17:02.520
What is it, Hori-san?

17:04.450 --> 17:05.710
Nothing.

17:12.490 --> 17:14.960
Sorry, I was daydreaming.

17:14.960 --> 17:16.680
Are you okay?

17:16.680 --> 17:19.450
What's got you so spaced out?

17:21.910 --> 17:23.550
All of...

17:23.550 --> 17:26.920
All of the coincidences that had to 
happen to make this moment possible.

17:27.490 --> 17:31.480
If even one hadn't happen, the world 
might be completely different.

17:35.410 --> 17:36.730
If that's true...

17:37.890 --> 17:42.950
Maybe it was destiny
that brought us together like this.

17:44.820 --> 17:46.120
Maybe.

17:47.870 --> 17:51.160
<i>I bet that no matter what we'd done,</i>

17:53.950 --> 17:55.660
<i>we would have found each other.</i>

17:56.380 --> 17:58.630
<b>Katagiri High School 63rd Graduation Ceremony</b>

18:03.200 --> 18:07.600
<i>Every day was new and different.</i>

18:08.220 --> 18:10.640
<i>I won't pretend I remember all of it.</i>

18:12.150 --> 18:16.400
<i>Most of the memories have
 faded and vanished,</i>

18:16.400 --> 18:19.400
<i>but many are just as vivid 
as the day they happened.</i>

18:19.400 --> 18:20.400
<b>Katagiri High School 63rd Graduation Ceremony</b>

18:20.450 --> 18:22.660
<b>Katagiri High School 63rd Graduation Ceremony</b>

18:22.070 --> 18:26.380
<i>I'm sure they're always going to be.</i>

18:22.700 --> 18:24.910
<b>Katagiri High School 63rd Graduation Ceremony</b>

18:24.950 --> 18:26.910
<b>Katagiri High School 63rd Graduation Ceremony</b>

18:28.660 --> 18:31.380
<i>And starting now...</i>

18:33.190 --> 18:34.170
Miyamura.

18:34.910 --> 18:37.410
We're going out for sushi today. Wanna come?

18:38.540 --> 18:39.670
Yeah!

18:39.670 --> 18:41.650
Okay! Let's go!

18:41.650 --> 18:43.370
Kyosuke will be glad to have you.

18:43.370 --> 18:44.400
He'll be obnoxious, of course.

18:44.400 --> 18:45.550
Great!

18:46.440 --> 18:48.140
<i>We're closer than before.</i>

18:48.700 --> 18:54.220
<i>We used to be so shy we couldn't 
look each other in the eye.</i>

18:55.310 --> 18:57.870
<i>But now we can laugh together</i>

18:58.370 --> 19:00.430
<i>and touch, even 
without a particular reason.</i>

19:02.320 --> 19:08.080
<i>I don't really know what 
we're thinking when we do.</i>

19:08.640 --> 19:10.940
<i>Even now, I'm still not sure.</i>

19:12.190 --> 19:15.240
<i>Saying "life" feels a little overblown.</i>

19:15.240 --> 19:17.440
<i>You might laugh at that.</i>

19:18.340 --> 19:24.340
<i>But if we can walk the path ahead together,</i>

19:24.340 --> 19:26.760
<i>I think that would be so wonderful.</i>

19:28.760 --> 19:31.640
<i>When you look down at your own shadow,</i>

19:31.640 --> 19:35.340
<i>don't forget that I'm by your side.</i>

19:36.310 --> 19:40.210
<i>Don't forget that there's 
a light shining on you.</i>

19:41.470 --> 19:43.880
<i>And when I hang my head,</i>

19:43.880 --> 19:46.050
<i>I'd like you to remind me</i>

19:47.780 --> 19:49.840
<i>that I'm not alone.</i>

19:50.680 --> 19:52.160
<i>Tell me.</i>

19:55.550 --> 19:57.350
<i>Hey, Miyamura.</i>

19:57.350 --> 19:59.420
<i>The sky looks so blue today.</i>

20:01.170 --> 20:03.670
<i>It feels like we could go wherever we want.</i>

20:07.790 --> 20:10.140
<i>I've never known the world like this.</i>

20:12.180 --> 20:17.190
<i>I never knew there was 
something so steadfast inside me.</i>

20:25.280 --> 20:27.880
Come on, Miyamura!

20:32.370 --> 20:35.870
<i>Look how pretty the cherry 
blossoms are, Miyamura.</i>

20:36.260 --> 20:38.000
<i>There's a gentle breeze.</i>

20:38.830 --> 20:42.140
<i>Thank you for helping me see so much.</i>

20:42.650 --> 20:43.680
<i>I'm overjoyed.</i>

20:45.080 --> 20:48.400
<i>The words to describe it would be
so ephemeral they might just fly away.</i>

20:48.930 --> 20:51.710
<i>So, just like the petals falling around us,</i>

20:51.710 --> 20:55.980
<i>I want to take my time letting you know.</i>

22:31.990 --> 22:36.000
<b>Journey
Katagiri High School</b>

22:34.470 --> 22:35.620
<i>Miyamura?</i>

22:36.000 --> 22:38.500
<i>Oh, sorry. Were you asleep?</i>

22:39.250 --> 22:41.920
No, I'm awake.

22:42.250 --> 22:43.630
It's okay.

22:43.970 --> 22:44.960
Really?

22:45.560 --> 22:46.570
Yeah.

22:47.190 --> 22:48.180
Okay.

22:48.800 --> 22:53.140
I'm not sure I get why,
but I just need to come, right?

22:53.600 --> 22:56.810
Okay.

23:02.610 --> 23:08.170
<i>Shortcake, Mont Blanc crêpes, 
cheesecake, choux cream...</i>

23:10.470 --> 23:12.410
Okay, I'm ready!

23:10.470 --> 23:14.160
<b>Fell back asleep!!</b>

23:12.410 --> 23:14.160
<b>4 hours late</b>

23:14.830 --> 23:17.430
Hey, it's my bro!

23:17.430 --> 23:20.270
H-H-H-H-Hori-san?

23:20.270 --> 23:22.610
She was saying you're really late.

23:23.650 --> 23:25.420
Oh, is that all?

23:25.890 --> 23:28.110
We had our graduation ceremony yesterday,

23:28.110 --> 23:31.050
so we were gonna take it easy today.

23:31.870 --> 23:33.630
I brought some cakes. Want one?

23:33.630 --> 23:34.960
Cake?

23:34.960 --> 23:36.060
Do you have chocolate?

23:36.060 --> 23:38.700
Oops... No, sorry.

23:39.830 --> 23:41.150
You're here, Miyamura.

23:41.080 --> 23:42.460
<b><i>JOLT</i></b>

23:43.760 --> 23:46.310
Y-Yes! Sorry for being late.

23:46.310 --> 23:48.340
I, uh, brought cake!

23:49.430 --> 23:52.930
Maybe we can all have some...

23:53.110 --> 23:55.070
<b>Silence</b>

23:53.900 --> 23:55.090
<i>Is she angry?</i>

23:56.020 --> 23:57.040
Okay.

23:57.930 --> 24:01.570
Great. I'll go get some plates.

24:01.570 --> 24:03.090
I'll bring the cakes.

24:05.830 --> 24:06.840
Hori-san?

24:07.300 --> 24:09.840
I've never done this before.

24:10.640 --> 24:11.860
What?

24:11.860 --> 24:14.790
Hey, can I have the strawberry one?

24:14.790 --> 24:17.280
Oh, sure. Whichever you like.

24:27.650 --> 24:29.620
Wh-What do you think?

24:30.360 --> 24:32.610
She gave up the girly style!

24:32.630 --> 24:34.130
It looks great!

24:34.130 --> 24:37.280
L-Liar! You hesitated!

24:37.280 --> 24:40.010
I mean it! It looks really great on you!

24:39.990 --> 24:42.890
They didn't understand what I asked for!

24:39.990 --> 24:47.000
<b>About this long</b>

24:42.890 --> 24:45.810
I didn't think they'd cut it this short!

24:45.810 --> 24:47.600
Easy, easy...

24:47.600 --> 24:49.800
You look cute with short hair.

24:52.050 --> 24:57.530
I wanted you to be the first person 
to see it. That's why I called you.

24:58.140 --> 25:00.180
I look like a boy.

25:00.180 --> 25:01.540
Are you sure you don't mind?

25:04.560 --> 25:06.540
I was thinking of getting a haircut, too.

25:07.530 --> 25:08.960
Liar.

25:08.960 --> 25:10.170
No, it's true.

25:13.970 --> 25:16.340
Dad, we got cake!

25:16.340 --> 25:18.680
Oh, it's Kyosuke. Welcome home.

25:18.680 --> 25:20.180
Yeah...

25:20.730 --> 25:23.500
What gives? Are you breaking up?

25:24.090 --> 25:25.400
Where'd that come from?

25:26.390 --> 25:28.690
Miyamura-kun, did something happen?

25:28.690 --> 25:31.800
I went to the salon where 
Hori-san usually goes.

25:31.800 --> 25:34.260
So it's no big deal?

25:34.830 --> 25:38.760
She wanted to normalize our hair lengths.

25:38.760 --> 25:41.620
Gals and guys can have their hair
however long they want.

25:41.620 --> 25:43.500
She gets hung up on the weirdest stuff.

25:43.500 --> 25:44.210
What was that?

25:44.210 --> 25:46.610
She paid to have it done.

25:46.610 --> 25:48.020
Oh?

25:48.450 --> 25:51.540
Kyoko-chan, your dad 
might need a haircut, too.

25:51.540 --> 25:53.150
Okay, then cut it.

25:53.150 --> 25:54.030
So cold!

25:54.520 --> 25:58.230
I've never had my hair this short 
before, so it's kinda funny.

25:58.230 --> 26:00.660
Feels awkward, does it?

26:00.660 --> 26:01.950
A little...

26:04.110 --> 26:07.670
When I'm with Hori-san, I get to 
have all sorts of new experiences.

26:07.670 --> 26:10.340
It's great that you and Kyoko match.

26:10.340 --> 26:12.450
Maybe I really should get a haircut.

26:12.450 --> 26:14.320
Should I cut it for you?

26:14.320 --> 26:15.600
Maybe not.

26:15.600 --> 26:17.000
Hori-san!
